1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:03,030
(Howard:)Hmm.

2
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:08,000
(Penny(spits out drink explosively. Howard types. Robot arm hands Penny a napkin):)Thank you
for driving me.

3
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,660
(Penny:)You're welcome.

4
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:13,190
(Sheldon:)I wish you weren't
wearing flip-flops.

5
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:15,760
(Sheldon:)It's dangerous
to drive in flip-flops.

6
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,800
(Leonard:)Sheldon.
Sorry.

7
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,770
(Sheldon:)I just don't want to be
yet another flip-flop fatality.

8
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:24,890
(Penny:)Can I ask you
a question?

9
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:27,470
(Sheldon:)Given your
community college education,

10
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,980
(Sheldon:)I encourage you to ask me
as many as possible.

11
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,860
(Leonard:)Yeah.
Well, my question is--

12
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:36,520
(Penny:)and I'm pretty sure
I know the answer--

13
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,520
(Penny:)is this your first date?

14
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:40,370
(Sheldon:)That depends.

15
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:42,570
(Sheldon:)Does square-dancing
with my sister

16
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:45,360
(Sheldon:)at a Teens for Jesus
Fourth of July Hoedown

17
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,660
(Sheldon:)count as a date?

18
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:48,160
(Howard:)No.

19
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,550
(Sheldon:)Then, this is my first date.

20
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,330
(Penny:)Okay. Well, then,
there's a couple of things

21
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:54,600
(Penny:)you should probably know.

22
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,040
(Sheldon:)I have a master's degree
and two doctorates.

23
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:01,760
(Sheldon:)The things I should know,
I do know.

